### XX Global Open Synchronous Championship

# Season 2022–2023

#DATE Leg III (04.11 — 13.11.2022)

# Notes for the reader:

# Please familiarize yourself with the question pack set before the game.

# Words in capital letters (e.g., X, FIRST, IT, DO THIS) should be emphasized when reading out loud. After reading the answer, you should also read out other accepted answers and the commentary to the question. Reading out the name(s) of the author(s) is advisable but not necessary.

# Additional notes for the reader are placed in square brackets before some of the questions. You must not read them out loud.

# Phonetic transcriptions of selected words (in square brackets) are put within the text of some questions for the reader’s convenience.

# Handouts for questions 11 and 35 are placed before the text of the questions. Please give the teams some time to familiarise themselves with the handouts, but do not read them out loud.

# Good luck!

## Block 1

# Edited by Yulia Didbaridze [did-bah-RID-zeh]

# The editor thanks the following people for testing the questions: Sergei Grigoriev [gree-GOR-yeff], Natalia Komar, Yuri Motkin, Maxim Merzlyakov [mers-lyah-KOFF], Sergei Terentyev [te-RENT-yeff], Andrei & Anastasia Tsepaev [tse-PIE-eff], and the teams «Absolutnoe menshinstvo» [abso-LUTE-noh-yeh men-shins-TVOH], «Guliay rvanina» [goo-LYAY rvah-NEE-nah] and «Krainiaya sbornaya» [CRY-nya-yuh ZBORE-nah-yuh]

? Initially, the creators of Netflix wanted to use the bleating of a goat, which would be a reference to THIS. Identify THIS using a palindrome.
! the MGM opening logo [accept any answers that mention MGM]
/ Instead of the now-iconic «tu-dum» sound, episodes could have been introduced by the bleating of a goat, which would be a reference to the MGM lion’s roar. However, later the Netflix founders said that they were happy to have dropped this idea.
^ https://www.20k.org/episodes/netflix
@ Yulia Didbaridze

? In the mid-19th century, a rich heir Roger Tichborne was travelling on a ship that disappeared. Later, the lack of an anchor helped Tichborne’s family prove in court that it was not Roger, who had apparently survived, but actually an impostor. It is believed that this court case popularised… WHAT?
! tattoos [acceptable answer: tattoo]
/ Roger followed the sailors’ custom and got a tattoo with a heart and an anchor. The impostor did not have such a tattoo. After that case tattoos became widespread among the general populace.
^ 
- https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/law-and-social-justice/news/articles/how-tattoos-became-fashionable-in-victorian-england/
- https://collections.countway.harvard.edu/onview/items/show/13074
@ Yulia Didbaridze

? Marshall Islands are a winding chain of atolls and islands with curved coastlines. Local seafarers used to say that the best method to find one’s way was using THEM, and in dangerous situations would lie down on the canoe’s floor in order to determine which island is the nearest. What are THEY?
! waves
/ Such natural conditions are conducive to the emergence of unique wave patterns around each island, and local navigators could determine their position by these patterns.
^ 
- https://www.smithsonianmag.com/arts-culture/science-and-tradition-are-resurrecting-lost-art-wave-piloting-180958005/
- https://skifiabook.ru/store/psihologiya-medicina/item_112.html
@ Yulia Didbaridze

? In the latter half of the 19th century, French intellectuals, appalled by the prevalence of criminals in research, founded the Society of Mutual Improvement. In order to help with later studies, the members would write an essay about their character upon joining the Society. Which word in the Society’s name did we substitute?
! autopsy [accepted answer: post-mortem]
/ The scientists were appalled by the fact that in medicine all important conclusions were based on autopsies of criminals and proposed to solve this issue with their own efforts.
^ https://mindhacks.com/2014/02/21/the-society-of-mutual-autopsy/
@ Yulia Didbaridze

? In order to draw attention to a widespread social evil, a certain company launched a line of alcoholic beverages with names such as Rachel, Carol, and Irene. Which ADJECTIVE did we omit in the text of this question several times?
! Bloody
/ The line of beers called Bloody Women was intended to draw attention to the issue of domestic abuse. The name was based on the famous cocktail, the Bloody Mary.
^ https://www.thedrinksbusiness.com/2021/11/female-hk-brewers-launch-beer-to-raise-awareness-on-domestic-abuse
@ Yulia Didbaridze

? Dugu Xin [Doo-goo SHIN], a 6th-century Chinese official, held several positions at the same time and was active in all of them. The man who found X that used to belong to Dugu Xin, at first thought it was a gambling die. What is X?
! seal of office [accept any answer that mentions a seal]
/ Dugu Xin worked with official papers and, for the sake of convenience, didn’t carry around many seals for each of his offices, but rather had them made into one, which had 26 faces.
^ 
- https://inf.news/en/collect/9f79b7d701cb62b8d04b23cd39299daf.html
- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dugu_Xin
@ Yulia Didbaridze

? Having learned about a visit by the higher-ups, some officials in a rural district of China handed out big white sacks to children. The sacks were to play the role of THIS. Who uses THIS in a common saying?
! wolf
/ THIS stands for «a sheep’s clothing» or a sheep’s coat of wool. The children were to stand in the fields, wearing the white sacks, and look like sheep. This way the officials wanted to paint a picture of prosperity in their district.
^ https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/asia_pacific/chinas-xi-tells-grumbling-party-cadres-dont-talk-back/2015/12/27/a6b25d2c-a446-11e5-8318-bd8caed8c588_story.html
@ Yulia Didbaridze

? A device developed by Leanne Wijnsma [Leh-AHN-neh VINE-smah], that warns about data leaks, needs to be filled up and then connected to a phone or a laptop. Its creator believes that this works faster than a sound signal, and compares data to X. What is X?
! gas [accepted answers: methane, natural gas]
/ When there is a leak threat, the device starts emitting a pungent odour. Its creator was inspired by warning systems in cooking stoves, in which natural gas is mixed with an unpleasant smelling mercaptan to help people notice the leak.
^ https://smellofdata.com/
@ Yulia Didbaridze

? In the ancient Egyptian tale, The Doomed Prince, the main character receives a prophecy and then a house is built for him in the desert. However, he leaves that house and eventually meets his fate. It is thought that this tale influenced the fate of a certain captain. WHO was this captain?
! James Hook [accepted answers: Captain Hook, Hook]
/ The protagonist is prophesied to die in a crocodile’s maw, so his parents try to send him away from danger. It has been proposed that the crocodile that pursues Captain Hook in Peter Pan, was inspired by this tale.
^ https://arzamas.academy/mag/910-help
@ Yulia Didbaridze

? In the opera Gould’s Wall, the protagonist wants to reach the same level of perfection as the great pianist Glenn Gould. The seats in the theatre hall are set at an angle for better comfort, and the performer must wear THIS on her feet while on stage. What is THIS?
! [rock] climbing shoes
/ The creators of this opera wanted to literalize the metaphor about «reaching the pinnacle of accomplishment», so that throughout the performance the main character climbs a vertical wall in full climbing gear, and manages to sing all the while.
^ 
- https://tapestryopera.com/performances/goulds-wall/
- https://www.thestar.com/entertainment/music/2022/07/29/the-opera-goulds-wall-has-the-soprano-climbing-an-18-metre-rock-wall.html
@ Yulia Didbaridze

? Handout
(img 2022-2023_III_en_001.png)
A Slow Year is a videogame, in which the player needs to wait for a leaf to fall from a tree in autumn and look at fresh snow in winter. Each part of the game opens with THIS. You have been given THIS in a comic strip format. What is THIS?
! haiku [accepted answer: hokku]
/ The game does not require any active input from the player and has a contemplative mood, which is enhanced by the instructions written as haiku. The author of this strip visualized a haiku through the proportions of the panels and the number of raindrops.
^ 
- https://kotaku.com/what-if-a-video-game-was-poetry-453104628
- https://mattmadden.com/2013/06/20/haiku-comics/
@ Yulia Didbaridze

? Each participant of a festival taking place in Colorado receives a t-shirt. In order to put the shirt on during a competition, they carefully strike and crease it first, while trying not to tear it off. The festival is dedicated to Bredo Morstuhl whose loving gransdon is an advocate of THIS. Name THIS using a word derived from Greek.
! cryonics [accept cryopreservation and any other word with cryo-]
/ The t-shirts are frozen, just like the man to whom the festival is dedicated. The event also includes plunging in freezing cold water and bowling with a frozen turkey. This way, one dead old guy became a cause for celebration for many people.
^ https://youtu.be/4MzGrNOqB5I
@ Yulia Didbaridze

## Block 2

#EDITOR Edited by: Yuri Razumov [RAH-zoom-off]

# Questions tested by: Artyom Guletsky [goo-LETS-key], Andrei Zabavin [zah-BAH-vin], Irina Kolesnikova [caw-LESS-nick-oh-vuh], Eugene Mirotin [mee-RAW-tin], Vera Monina [MAW-nee-nuh].

? The first edition of Johann Fichte’s [FICK-tay] first book was published without any mention of the author’s name, only stating the city where it was written. The book received wide acclaim, and then a famous individual had to make a statement. In Which city did Fichte write the book?
! Koenigsberg [accepted answers: Kralovec, Kaliningrad]
/ A philosophical treatise written in Koenigsberg was immediately believed to be a new work by Kant (who lived there and had not published anything for a long time). However, the book got its reputation on merit, not only due to his presumed authorship, and when Kant made it clear that the author was not him, but Fichte, the latter was offered tenure at the Jena University.
^ Andrea Wulf, Magnificent Rebels.
@ Yuri Razumov

? Who knows where an arrow will land when it is shot from a bow? In a novel by Philip Jose Farmer, the Dokalians use the depiction of a bow and arrow as an analogue for THIS. What is THIS?
! Question mark. [accepted answer: ?]
/ Until the arrow has hit its target, it can be seen as a symbol of uncertainty. Unlike the Dothraki in George Martin’s series, the Dokalians did not have a full-fledged artificial language. Curiously Philip Jose Farmer wrote this novel under the pseudonym Kilgore Trout, a fictional writer from Kurt Vonnegut’s books, so that some reviewers believed the book was by Vonnegut.
^ Philip Jose Farmer, Venus on The Half-Shell.
@ Yuri Razumov

? In a long historical novel by Anthony Burgess, a character notes that changes have affected not only the British royal family, but also Henry James, who stopped walking his X. Identify the X.
! Dachshund. [accepted answers: Dachs, sausage dog, wiener dog]
/ After the outbreak of the First World War, the British royal dynasty dropped its German name Saxe-Coburg-Gotha and became the Windsors. In Britain, dachshunds were seen as German and featured heavily in propaganda (however, the stories about them being deliberately killed are a myth). The famous writer Henry James did indeed have a dachshund, named Max, but most probably he just stopped taking particularly long walks where he could be easily seen with the dog. James dedicated much of his time to Britain’s war effort (and even became a British citizen), and Max was 11 years old at that time, which is quite a lot for a dog.
^ Anthony Burgess, Earthly Powers.
@ Yuri Razumov

? Even seemingly identical objects can have different magnetic properties. In a system proposed by Martin Lauer, a sensor placed on THIS measures the magnetic profile directly underneath, and a specially prepared map enhances the GPS, increasing safety. What is THIS?
! train. [accepted answers: locomotive, train engine]
/ GPS is not precise enough to distinguish between adjacent rail tracks, while tunnels interfere with satellite connection Even though all rails look identical, modern sensors are capable of identifying them by their magnetic profiles, which allows to make a precise map of the tracks and use it for safer and more efficient scheduling.
^ 
- https://www.economist.com/science-and-technology/2022/09/28/keeping-trains-apart-is-crucial-to-safety
- https://www.itk-engineering.de/en/story/magnetic-railway-onboard-sensor/
@ Yuri Razumov

? In 2007, a replica of a Phoenician ship was built in the Middle East that later proved capable of crossing the ocean. Today this replica is kept in a landlocked US state because in 2021 the ship was bought by THEM. Who are THEY?
! Mormons [accepted answers: The Church of Latter-Day Saints, the Latter-Day Saints, the LDS Church]
/ The ship reached America under its own power. The researchers first demonstrated that a 5th century BCE Phoenician ship could plausibly sail along the African continent to the equator (a fact possibly mentioned by Herodotus), and then sailed from Tunisia to Florida. According to the Book of Mormon, a group of Israelites reached America soon after the fall of Jerusalem to the Babylonians, and so modern Mormons have an understandable interest in ancient ocean-going ships.
^ 
- https://web.archive.org/web/20220713100707/https://twitter.com/cwjones89/status/1547160424759451650
- https://www.phoenicia.rocks/
@ Yuri Razumov

? Many Ancient Roman epigrams had salacious subject matter and often contained insults. Having studied these and other ancient sources, 18th-century scholar Jean Astruc came to the correct conclusion that THIS appeared in Europe only in the late 15th century. What is THIS?
! syphilis.
/ Many Roman epigrams openly describe sexual acts, and insulting verses would certainly have featured references to a disease like syphilis, had the Romans known it. However, neither satirists nor historians or the Bible mention such symptoms. Astruc collated this fact and the descriptions by 15th-century doctors concluding that syphilis first reached Europe as a result of Columbus’s voyages.
^ 
- The Cambridge Companion to Erotic Literature.
- Jean Astruc, De Morbus Veneris (https://archive.org/details/b30531093_0002/page/66/mode/2up)
@ Yuri Razumov

? An article describing the periodic necessity of THIS is illustrated with a picture of a spinning figure skater. Thawing and freezing glaciers are compared to the skater’s arms. Identify THIS, using two words exactly.
! leap second.
/ When ice caps on mountain peaks thaw and freeze again, this affects the speed of the Earth’s rotation. In a similar way, but much more drastically, figure skaters can change the speed of their own rotation by adjusting the position of their arms. The inaccuracies in time measurements accumulate progressively, so that from time to time a leap second must be added to a year. Figure skaters are known to leap a lot.
^ https://engineering.fb.com/2022/07/25/production-engineering/its-time-to-leave-the-leap-second-in-the-past/
@ Yuri Razumov

? The only things the 5-year-old Samuel Seymour remembered from that evening were a tall man and another man leaping from a very high place. In 1956, then elderly Seymour took part in a TV show called I’ve Got a Secret. What was his secret?
! He witnessed Lincoln’s assassination [accept all answers that mention Abraham Lincoln’s death].
/ Seymour’s family attended the performance of Our American Cousin, during which Abraham Lincoln was assassinated. Sam was shown where the President was seated (and Lincoln was famously 193 cm tall). Having shot Lincoln, John Wilkes Booth jumped from the box onto the stage and escaped; the boy mostly remembered the leap, and not the shots. In 1956, as the last surviving witness of the event, Seymour took part in a TV show.
^ https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samuel_J._Seymour
@ Yuri Razumov

? Contrary to conspiracy theories, global warming is a real issue. Research has shown that THESE THINGS can have different effects depending on weather and time of day, and now an enterprise called Satavia is developing schedules that would take this fact into account. What are THESE THINGS?
! contrails [accepted answer: condensation trails, vapour trails].
/ On the one hand, contrails contain greenhouse gases, but on the other hand, they can reflect sunlight. Understanding which of the two effects is stronger in what conditions, can help build flight schedules that would mitigate the deleterious effects of flying planes. According to a popular conspiracy, contrails are formed when mind-control substances are dispersed from planes.
^ https://medium.datadriveninvestor.com/reducing-contrails-by-rerouting-aircraft-957a95f51d67
@ Yuri Razumov

? While watching a documentary about Liverpool FC, one finds that the Spaniard Pepe Reina and the Brazilian Lucas Leiva don’t need THIS, unlike the Liverpool-born Jamie Carragher. What is THIS?
! subtitles [accepted answer: subs, captions].
/ Scouse accent is harder to understand than Brazilian or Spanish one. So the movie that was made for US viewers had subtitles only in scenes that feature Carragher.
^ https://metro.co.uk/2012/10/12/jamie-carragher-given-subtitles-in-tv-documentary-being-liverpool-598968/
@ Yuri Razumov

? In the 16th century Joachim du Bellay wrote that some of his contemporaries saw science and poetry as if they were holy relics, kept behind a glass. Du Bellay wrote a treatise defending THIS. Identify THIS.
! the French language.
/ In the 16th century many still believed that both scientific works and works of poetry can be written only in Latin or Greek, which were as dead as saints’ relics (usually parts of their dead bodies). Du Bellay and other poets in La Pleiade group wrote in French.
^ 
- Walter Pater, The Renaissance: Studies in Art and Poetry. https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/2398/pg2398-images.html
- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Défense_et_illustration_de_la_langue_française
@ Yuri Razumov

? Yellow-legged frogs live in mountain streams. To prepare captive-bred frogs for release, Talisin Hammond used THIS. Which surname is often associated with THIS?
! Jacuzzi.
/ Swimming against the current is hard, and captive-bred frogs need to train for that. Water streams in a jacuzzi bath are like a treadmill for them.
^ https://www.economist.com/science-and-technology/2022/06/01/the-health-giving-benefits-of-jacuzzis-for-frogs
@ Yuri Razumov

